Basically the flow for OAuth 2.0 is.

(1) Client → API Gateway → OAuth Server (Auth Service) → Issues Access Token & Refresh Token
(2) Client sends Access Token → API Gateway validates it → Calls Microservice
(3) Microservice extracts user roles/permissions from the token and enforces authorization.


Detailed -

1️⃣ Client Logs In

Sends credentials to the API Gateway.
The API Gateway forwards the request to the OAuth Authorization Server (Spring Authorization Server).
OAuth Server issues an Access Token & Refresh Token.
2️⃣ Client Calls API Gateway with Access Token

Sends the Access Token in the request.
API Gateway validates the token (either locally or by calling the OAuth Server).
3️⃣ API Gateway Forwards the Request to Microservices

If the token is valid, the API Gateway forwards the request with the token to the target microservice.
Microservices extract user roles & permissions from the token to enforce RBAC or ACLs.
